    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="26.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Wi">Wi</ref> 26.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26.1" corresp="#wit-h">Se þe hine gefo ⁊ gegange, healfne hine age; gif hine man cwelle, geselle heom man LXX scll'.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#oliver" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-h">Se þe hine gefo ⁊ gegange, healfne hine age. Gif hine man cwelle, geselle heom man LXX scƚƚ.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h">He who seizes and delivers him [the thief], owns him half; if he [the thief] is killed, let them be paid 70 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">He who catches and secures him, shall have half his value. If he is put to death, 70 shillings shall be paid to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Der welcher ihn fasst und stellt, besitze ihn zur Hälfte; wenn man jenen tödtet, so gebe man ihm [dem Einfänger] 70 Schll.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The one who seizes and holds him is to have half of him; if he is killed, let [the captor] be given 70 shillings.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
